WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:05.825
The Purdue Model matters because industrial operations depend on several kinds of systems working together.

00:00:05.825 --> 00:00:08.496
Enterprise planning may create a production schedule.

00:00:08.496 --> 00:00:11.168
Site operations translate that demand into work.

00:00:11.168 --> 00:00:14.221
Supervisory systems provide operator visibility, controllers execute logic,

00:00:14.221 --> 00:00:16.893
and field instruments interact with the process.

00:00:16.893 --> 00:00:21.473
A failure or compromise can move through these dependencies even when the

00:00:21.473 --> 00:00:23.381
systems belong to different teams.

00:00:23.381 --> 00:00:27.579
Placing functions into levels helps identify where connectivity should be limited.

00:00:27.579 --> 00:00:32.159
Traffic that stays within a control area has a different purpose from

00:00:32.159 --> 00:00:34.449
data being transferred to enterprise analytics.

00:00:34.449 --> 00:00:39.029
The model supports segmentation by showing where trust changes and where controlled

00:00:39.029 --> 00:00:40.937
intermediary services may be appropriate.

00:00:40.937 --> 00:00:42.845
It also supports risk analysis.

00:00:42.845 --> 00:00:47.043
Systems near the process may have direct safety and reliability consequences.

00:00:47.043 --> 00:00:51.623
Systems higher in the architecture may have broader user populations, internet dependencies,

00:00:51.623 --> 00:00:53.913
and exposure to common enterprise threats.

00:00:53.913 --> 00:00:58.493
Neither is automatically more important; their risk comes from different functions, pathways,

00:00:58.493 --> 00:00:59.638
and operational effects.

00:00:59.638 --> 00:01:01.928
The model improves communication between disciplines.

00:01:01.928 --> 00:01:05.745
Security teams can explain why direct enterprise-to-controller access creates risk.

00:01:05.745 --> 00:01:10.706
Engineers can explain why a control flow requires low latency or high availability.

00:01:10.706 --> 00:01:13.759
Operators can identify which systems provide essential visibility.

00:01:13.759 --> 00:01:17.957
These conversations turn an abstract network diagram into an operational architecture.

00:01:17.957 --> 00:01:21.392
Finally, Purdue helps distinguish data flow from control flow.

00:01:21.392 --> 00:01:25.209
Production data may move upward for reporting, while commands, recipes,

00:01:25.209 --> 00:01:28.262
or configuration changes move downward under stricter authority.

00:01:28.262 --> 00:01:30.934
Reviewing both directions reveals remote access, update,

00:01:30.934 --> 00:01:34.750
and administration paths that a simple data-flow discussion might miss.

00:01:34.750 --> 00:01:40.093
The goal is not to prevent communication, but to make every cross-level flow necessary,

00:01:40.093 --> 00:01:41.620
controlled, observable, and owned.
